WEBVTT

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:07.850
Seattle. October, 1947. The war's been over two years, and the city still hasn't slept.

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:09.350
Neither have I.

00:00:10.367 --> 00:00:16.200
The files on my desk are neat. Everything else about this case is not.

00:00:16.867 --> 00:00:21.033
Upstairs, the evidence room. Somebody left gaps on those shelves.

00:00:21.967 --> 00:00:28.217
A photograph. Two men, a truck, and half a license plate. Somebody saw the rest.

00:00:31.133 --> 00:00:36.133
A cipher wheel. Twenty-six settings, and only one of them is English.

00:00:38.133 --> 00:00:40.633
A password. A pier. An hour.

00:00:42.767 --> 00:00:48.600
Everyone in this town knows one piece. Nobody wants to hand over the rest.

00:00:49.933 --> 00:00:54.517
A motorman, eight months from his pension, slips me a note.

00:00:55.767 --> 00:00:58.267
The rain took the last digit.

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:05.883
Three people. Three pieces of one license plate. Put them together.

00:01:07.733 --> 00:01:12.317
I keep a casebook. What I know, and what's still open.

00:01:14.733 --> 00:01:18.900
The waterfront talks to bartenders before it talks to detectives.

00:01:21.133 --> 00:01:25.717
So I find it myself. Sweep the dial in the dark.

00:01:26.167 --> 00:01:29.083
Close isn't good enough. Until it is.

00:01:30.533 --> 00:01:33.867
Under Pioneer Square, the city buried its mistakes.

00:01:34.133 --> 00:01:38.717
Pitch dark. If grues made it to Seattle, they're down here.

00:01:38.933 --> 00:01:41.850
Then somebody starts tapping on a pipe.

00:01:44.733 --> 00:01:49.317
Pier Seven. After midnight. Everything I've got is in my pockets.

00:01:49.533 --> 00:01:52.450
Is it enough? That's up to you.

00:01:53.333 --> 00:01:56.667
Emerald Shadows. A noir detective game. Seattle, 1947.

00:01:56.933 --> 00:01:58.183
Download it now.

